# imazen26 K300 real-image perf — port vs C, encode-only

date:   2026-09-17
commit: 55ae8530 (main tip; contains b47d8e9f dbgenv + 55ae8530 cost LUT)
host:   i265 (x86_64-linux, 20 logical cores, 30 GiB)
data:   benchmarks/imazen26_perf_2026-09-17.raw.tsv

WHAT. Encode-only wall-clock medians, port vs C reference, on 4 of the
20 K300 gate images (one per measured content class): a photo, a
synthetic line plot, a web screenshot, a bilevel patent scan.
512x512 centre crops, q32, bd8, presets 0/6/10/13 as listed.

METHOD. `identity_run "crop:<png>"` once to materialise the .yuv, then
port = `perf_encode raw:<yuv> 512 512 32 <preset> out 0` (no warmup
arg = single timed encode per process), C =
`capture_c_trace.bin 512 512 32 <preset> <yuv> c.obu 8`. Interleaved
paired iterations (port, C, port, C, ...), `date +%s%N` around each
process, median of N. NOT pinned to a P-core and NOT `perf stat`
instructions — wall-clock process medians; interleaving absorbs drift.
The encode itself is >99% of the process for every cell (harness setup
is a few ms of YUV read).

IDENTITY. Every (image, preset, bd) cell here passed the imazen26 gate
in the same session at the same commit — 40/40 byte-identical, all
streams aomdec-decodable. The timing cells are therefore byte-identical
cells, not approximations.

RESULT. Every real-image cell is inside the 50% bound — range
1.07x..1.23x across classes and presets. The worst synthetic cell
(512x512 gradient p10 = 1.51x in perf_gap_lut-i265) does NOT
generalise: real content carries more coefficients per block, where
the port's C-faithful trellis/entropy cores dominate both sides
equally, while the flat gradient's near-empty txbs leave the port's
per-block fixed costs relatively exposed. Treat the gradient number
as a floor-content outlier, not the typical gap.

  image                     preset   port_ms   C_ms     ratio
  2001_people (photo)         0      5380.2    5022.4   1.071x
  2001_people (photo)         6        79.6      64.7   1.231x
  2001_people (photo)         10       15.2      13.6   1.121x
  7002_plots (line plot)      6        66.9      59.6   1.124x
  7002_plots (line plot)      10       20.9      18.3   1.141x
  8129_web-screenshots        10       11.1       9.7   1.147x
  8129_web-screenshots        13       11.3       9.5   1.179x
  6003_scans-patents (1bit)   6        23.1      19.1   1.211x
  6003_scans-patents (1bit)   10        9.1       7.7   1.194x
